# Copy to  tools\.discord-bot  and fill in. That file is gitignored.
#
# Used by tools\DiscordNotify.ps1 (release and patch announcements) and, for the token
# only, by the game server to read the guild's role NAMES so "dev" can mean something
# without anyone hunting for a role snowflake.
#
# The token is read at the moment it is needed and never stored in a config or logged.
# Point Discord.BotTokenFile in the server config at this file.
#
# A BOT TOKEN IS A PASSWORD, and a stronger one than a webhook URL: it grants everything
# the bot can reach, not just one channel. Never commit it. If one is ever pasted anywhere
# public, regenerate it in the Developer Portal immediately - rotating is free and cheap.

# From https://discord.com/developers/applications -> your app -> Bot -> Reset Token.
# Needs the "Server Members Intent" if you want role resolution.
token=PUT_THE_BOT_TOKEN_HERE

# Right-click the channel in Discord (with Developer Mode on) -> Copy Channel ID.
# This is where release announcements are posted.
channel=PUT_THE_CHANNEL_ID_HERE
